[:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bd2b79a-bc49-5c01-9237-4642e237863f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-82527"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-82525"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062905/assets/4229e1e8c92803a4d51043442a8bc65a6560e11a1e7559af7ec4246fe3005e75.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation that acts on vectors in ${R}^{2}$ as follows (in the order given):\n\n- it shears vectors by a shear factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$ in the $x$-direction, and then\n\n- rotates the result by $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians clockwise about the origin.\n\nWhat is the image of the unit square shown above under the action of the linear transformation?" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the shear by a shear factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$ in the $x$-direction:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062905/assets/c0dfba56ed4c0ceb0b1739304c562040a2a69044117665bba5bf4fc2f506044f.png)\n\nThen, we apply the rotation of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians clockwise:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062905/assets/ff3dca52efc6e985e500f22ce43658855c09901535378081ed6fc07d5bfec115.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-70642"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062905/assets/e966d34d56ae25deb6bbf5849e813493c51730981031955e6833fd04d9ec1e2a.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation that acts on vectors in ${R}^{2}$ as follows (in the order given):\n\n- it rotates vectors by ${90}^{∘}$ counterclockwise about the origin, and then\n\n- stretches the result by a scale factor of $2$ in the $x$-direction.\n\nWhat is the image of the unit square shown above under the action of the linear transformation?" :question/worked-soluti